@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Question kinds)

Every @@q kind, each one live. Answers are checked in the browser for feedback and again on the server for marks.

@section(Questions and quizzes)

@subsection(@@q)

A question or a blank.

@q(fn: 2.2, except=volt)

@q(fsi: violin, except=volt+units)

@q(units: W)

@q(mch: 3, *4, 5)

@q(f: Paris)

@q(fn: 3.9, 4.1)

@q answer @e

@q(4)

Worth 2 points, partial credit, with a penalty: @q(mav, *a, *b, c, pts=2, partial=0.5, penalty=0.25)

grading=all: @q(mav, *x, *y, z, grading=all)

grading=any: @q(mav, *x, *y, z, grading=any)

grading=first: @q(mav, *x, *y, z, grading=first)

Options shuffled, labelled for @@qref: @q(mch, *4, 3, 5, shuffle, label=q-four)

One box per ;-part on paper: @q(f: 3;4, boxes)

A sized widget: @q(essay, w=420px, h=120px)

@subsection(@@quiz)

A quiz container — ONE question per line.

@quiz
2+2? @q(fn: 4)
@endquiz

@quiz(shuffle, numbered)
What is 3+4? @q(fn: 7)
What is 5-2? @q(fn: 3)
@endquiz

@subsection(@@likert5)

A Likert table: statements down the side, a 1–5 scale across.

@likert5
I enjoyed the course
@endlikert5

@likert5(scale=7, labels=Never|Rarely|Sometimes|Often|Usually|Almost always|Always)
I check my units
I draw the circuit first
@endlikert5

@section(Every kind)

Each line gives the kind, what it grades, and a live question.

@subsection(c)

exact answer

Answer: @q(c:answer)

@subsection(draw))

freehand sketch on a blank canvas — manually graded

Answer: @q(draw)

@subsection(e)

alias for eq — math answer, whitespace/case normalised

Answer: @q(e:answer)

@subsection(eq)

equation/math box (accepts forms); 'e:' is shorthand

Answer: @q(eq:form1 | form2)

@subsection(eq.expanded)

answer must be MULTIPLIED OUT — rejects (x+2)(x+1) copied back from the prompt

Answer: @q(eq.expanded:x^2+3x+2)

@subsection(eq.factored)

answer must be FACTORED — accepts (1+x)^2, rejects the expanded x^2+2x+1

Answer: @q(eq.factored:(x+1)(x+1))

@subsection(eq.min)

OPTIMAL (Karnaugh) answer: the same function, in the key's form (sum of products or product of sums), no more terms or literals — any equally small cover is right, a longer one is wrong (also eq.minimal, eq.optimal)

Answer: @q(eq.min:A'B'+A'C'+A'D)

@subsection(eq.reduced)

answer must be in LOWEST TERMS — rejects 2/6 and the un-evaluated 3/4+1/6

Answer: @q(eq.reduced:1/3)

@subsection(eq.strict)

no algebraic equivalence — exact normalized string

Answer: @q(eq.strict:x+1)

@subsection(essay)

essay with editable starter text

Answer: @q(essay: starter text)

@subsection(essay))

free-text essay

Answer: @q(essay)

@subsection(essay500.store)

written survey answer: OCR-transcribed + recorded on scan grading, 0 points (also 'survey')

Answer: @q(essay500.store:)

@subsection(f)

or spell it out: case sensitive | space insensitive | insensitive

Answer: @q(f, New York, space insensitive)

@subsection(f)

text fill-in (exact, case-insensitive by default)

Answer: @q(f:answer)

@subsection(f)

any of the |-separated answers is correct (e.g. watt|watts)

Answer: @q(f:watt|watts)

@subsection(f.cs)

exact match, case matters (the strict form)

Answer: @q(f.cs:Answer)

@subsection(f72)

fill-in with a fixed box width (px)

Answer: @q(f72:answer)

@subsection(fc)

COMPLEX answer (real, imaginary, tolerance) — the student may type 3+4j or 5*exp(i*pi/6)

Answer: @q(fc, 3, 4, 0.01)

@subsection(fci)

case-insensitive (explicit; same as f)

Answer: @q(fci:answer)

@subsection(fcs)

the exact case is required — 'answer' does not match 'Answer' (same as f.cs)

Answer: @q(fcs:Answer)

@subsection(fcsi)

ignores both case and whitespace (explicit)

Answer: @q(fcsi:answer)

@subsection(fi)

ignores case AND whitespace (the loosest match)

Answer: @q(fi:answer)

@subsection(fi.min)

a fill-in that accepts ANY minimal cover of the same map, in any order (A'C'+B'C+AB here), and rejects a longer equivalent

Answer: @q(fi.min:A'B'+BC'+AC)

@subsection(fn)

numeric (range, value, or >20 / >=20 / <5 threshold)

Answer: @q(fn:lo,hi)

@subsection(formula)

symbolic/derived answer, graded like eq (algebraic equivalence)

Answer: @q(formula: V/R)

@subsection(fr)

regex answer

Answer: @q(fr:pattern)

@subsection(fsi)

ignores whitespace — 'ParisFrance' also matches

Answer: @q(fsi:Paris France)

@subsection(hmc)

alias of mch — multiple choice, options across the line

Answer: @q(hmc, *a, b, c)

@subsection(likert5))

5-point Likert scale

Answer: @q(likert5)

@subsection(m)

truth table: =given labels/inputs, _value = graded blank, bare _ = ungraded

Answer: @q(m:3,3: =A,=B,=AND, =0,=0,_0, =1,=1,_1)

@subsection(m)

matrix grid — graded cells are _value (e.g. _0); given/labels are =value; bare _ is ungraded

Answer: @q(m:2,2:_1,_0,_0,_1)

@subsection(m)

matrix grid (ungraded)

Answer: @q(m:2,3)

@subsection(mad)

select all that apply (multi-select list)

Answer: @q(mad: *a, *b, c, d)

@subsection(mah)

select all that apply (checkboxes, horizontal)

Answer: @q(mah: *a, *b, c, d)

@subsection(markdraw)

freehand marking OVER an image — circle the fault, annotate the diagram

Answer: @q(markdraw, src=circuit.svg)

@subsection(match)

cols=N lays the pairs out in N columns instead of one tall stack

Answer: @q(match, a=1, b=2, cols=2)

@subsection(match)

bare entries (no =) are DISTRACTORS: extra wrong choices in the answer bank

Answer: @q(match, a=1, b=2, distractor1, distractor2)

@subsection(match)

matching pairs — repeated right values dedupe in the bank

Answer: @q(match, term1=def1, term2=def2)

@subsection(mav)

select all that apply (checkboxes, vertical)

Answer: @q(mav: *a, *b, c, d)

@subsection(mcd)

multiple choice (dropdown)

Answer: @q(mcd, *correct, wrong1, wrong2)

@subsection(mch)

* correct · ~ partial 'more-correct' · plain wrong

Answer: @q(mch, *a, *b, ~0.5 c, d)

@subsection(mch)

multiple choice (horizontal)

Answer: @q(mch, *correct, wrong1, wrong2)

@subsection(mch)

policy: partial|proportional|jaccard|allornothing

Answer: @q(mch, grading=partial, penalty=1, *a, *b, c)

@subsection(mcv)

cols=N lays the choices out in N columns instead of one tall stack

Answer: @q(mcv, *correct, b, c, d, cols=2)

@subsection(mcv)

multiple choice (vertical)

Answer: @q(mcv, *correct, wrong1, wrong2)

@subsection(moddraw)

freehand over an image that starts with the author's own strokes loaded — the student modifies them

Answer: @q(moddraw, src=circuit.svg)

@subsection(mwidth)

matrix grid, fixed px size

Answer: @q(m200,120:2,2)

@subsection(n)

INTEGER answer (rejects 3.5); @@q(n, 1, 10) = integer in range

Answer: @q(n, 5)

@subsection(order)

put in order

Answer: @q(order, first, second, third)

@subsection(range)

answer is an interval; student types '3-5'. + mode=overlap|contains|within, tol=

Answer: @q(range, 3, 5)

@subsection(slider)

drag a slider to answer, graded within ±tol

Answer: @q(slider, min=0, max=100, answer=42, tol=2)

@subsection(unordered)

student lists all members in any order; partial credit; each member may use | alternatives

Answer: @q(unordered:red, white, blue)

@subsection(uo)

terse alias of unordered — all members, any order, partial credit

Answer: @q(uo: red, white, blue)

@subsection(uo3)

uo3: = any 3 of the accepted pool count; more never hurts; case-insensitive (.cs opts out, .si ignores spaces)

Answer: @q(uo3:AMD|Advanced Micro Devices, Intel, Nvidia, TSMC, Samsung)

@subsection(vmc)

alias of mcv — multiple choice, one option per line

Answer: @q(vmc, *a, b, c)

